    <h1>Job Application Summary Report</h1><h2>Overview</h2><p>This document provides a comprehensive summary of job applications tracked in "The Job Search Project" spreadsheet, covering applications from July 2025 through August 2025.</p><p></p><h2>Application Statistics</h2><h3>Total Applications: 245+</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Applied</strong>: 156 positions</p></li><li><p><strong>Rejected</strong>: 67 positions</p></li><li><p><strong>1st Interview</strong>: 8 positions</p></li><li><p><strong>Test</strong>: 1 position</p></li><li><p><strong>Not Applied</strong>: 13 positions</p></li></ul><h3>Application Status Breakdown</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Applied (63.7%)</strong>: 156 applications submitted and pending response</p></li><li><p><strong>Rejected (27.3%)</strong>: 67 applications that received rejection responses</p></li><li><p><strong>Interview Stage (3.3%)</strong>: 8 applications that progressed to first interview</p></li><li><p><strong>Other Statuses</strong>: Test, Not Applied, blank entries</p></li></ul><h2>Company Categories</h2><h3>Technology &amp; Software Companies</h3><p><strong>Major Tech Companies:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Meta, Google (Alphabet), Microsoft, Amazon</p></li><li><p>GitHub, GitLab, Atlassian, Docker</p></li><li><p>Figma, Notion, Vercel, Supabase</p></li><li><p>Discord, Twitch, Netflix</p></li></ul><p><strong>AI/ML Focused Companies:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Anthropic, OpenAI, Hugging Face</p></li><li><p>Scale AI, Databricks, Perplexity</p></li><li><p>Linear (AI), ClickUp (AI roles)</p></li><li><p>Sierra, Decagon, Norm AI</p></li></ul><p><strong>Fintech &amp; Crypto:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Coinbase, Kraken, Gemini, BitGo</p></li><li><p>Robinhood, Cash App, Plaid, Stripe</p></li><li><p>Circle, Anchorage, 0x</p></li><li><p>Ramp, Affirm, SoFi</p></li></ul><p><strong>Startups &amp; Emerging Companies:</strong></p><ul><li><p>YC Companies: Glimpse, GovDash, Heron Data</p></li><li><p>Early-stage: Meow, Bandana, ProSights</p></li><li><p>Growth-stage: Runway ML, Speechify, Retool</p></li></ul><h3>Traditional Industries</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Financial Services</strong>: Goldman Sachs, Morgan Stanley, Point72</p></li><li><p><strong>Media &amp; Entertainment</strong>: Sony Music, New York Times, Fandom</p></li><li><p><strong>Enterprise Software</strong>: Salesforce, Oracle, IBM, Cisco</p></li></ul><h2>Role Types Applied For</h2><h3>Software Engineering Roles (Primary Focus)</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Full Stack Engineer</strong>: 45+ applications</p></li><li><p><strong>Backend Engineer</strong>: 35+ applications</p></li><li><p><strong>Frontend Engineer</strong>: 25+ applications</p></li><li><p><strong>Platform Engineer</strong>: 20+ applications</p></li></ul><h3>Specialized Technical Roles</h3><ul><li><p><strong>AI/ML Engineer</strong>: 30+ applications</p></li><li><p><strong>DevOps/Infrastructure Engineer</strong>: 15+ applications</p></li><li><p><strong>Data Engineer</strong>: 10+ applications</p></li><li><p><strong>Mobile Engineer</strong>: 5+ applications</p></li></ul><h3>Experience Levels Targeted</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Senior Software Engineer</strong>: 85+ applications</p></li><li><p><strong>Software Engineer (Mid-level)</strong>: 60+ applications</p></li><li><p><strong>Staff/Principal Engineer</strong>: 15+ applications</p></li><li><p><strong>New Grad/Junior</strong>: 10+ applications</p></li></ul><h2>Geographic Distribution</h2><h3>Work Location Preferences</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Remote</strong>: 45+ positions</p></li><li><p><strong>Hybrid</strong>: 35+ positions</p></li><li><p><strong>On-site</strong>: 25+ positions</p></li><li><p><strong>New York City</strong>: Primary location focus</p></li><li><p><strong>San Francisco Bay Area</strong>: Secondary focus</p></li></ul><h2>Application Timeline</h2><h3>July 2025 (Peak Activity)</h3><ul><li><p><strong>July 10</strong>: 60+ applications (major application day)</p></li><li><p><strong>July 14</strong>: 45+ applications</p></li><li><p><strong>July 15</strong>: 25+ applications</p></li><li><p><strong>July 17</strong>: 30+ applications</p></li></ul><h3>August 2025 (Continued Activity)</h3><ul><li><p><strong>August 12-13</strong>: 40+ applications</p></li><li><p><strong>August 18-19</strong>: 15+ applications</p></li></ul><h2>Interview Progress</h2><h3>Companies with Interview Activity</h3><ol><li><p><strong>Meow</strong> - Full Stack Software Engineer (1st Interview scheduled 7/17)</p></li><li><p><strong>Speechify</strong> - Software Engineer, AI Studio (1st Interview 7/22)</p></li><li><p><strong>XAI</strong> - Software Engineering Specialist (Interview 8/18)</p></li><li><p><strong>Soma Capital</strong> - Full Stack Software Engineer (1 interview completed, rejected)</p></li><li><p><strong>Hexmodal</strong> - Junior Software Engineer (2 interviews completed, rejected)</p></li><li><p><strong>Dirac</strong> - Full Stack Software Engineer (1st Interview 8/19)</p></li><li><p><strong>Tivara</strong> - Product Engineer (Interview 7/22, rejected)</p></li><li><p><strong>Sony Music</strong> - Modern Workplace Technology Lead (1st Interview 8/20)</p></li></ol><h2>Recruiter Contacts</h2><h3>Active Recruiter Relationships</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Kimberly Owen</strong>: Meow, Bandana</p></li><li><p><strong>Drew Sussberg</strong>: Qrypt, Soma Capital, Sequence</p></li><li><p><strong>Henry Mills</strong>: Tivara, Othello, Soundmap</p></li><li><p><strong>Sonara</strong>: Automated application service (50+ applications)</p></li><li><p><strong>Ian Tushman</strong>: Dirac</p></li><li><p><strong>Guillian Eller</strong>: Fora</p></li></ul><h2>Notable Patterns &amp; Insights</h2><h3>High-Volume Application Days</h3><ul><li><p>Concentrated application efforts on specific dates</p></li><li><p>Mix of manual applications and automated submissions</p></li><li><p>Focus on similar role types across multiple companies</p></li></ul><h3>Company Preferences</h3><ul><li><p>Strong focus on high-growth tech companies</p></li><li><p>Emphasis on AI/ML and fintech sectors</p></li><li><p>Mix of established companies and startups</p></li><li><p>Geographic concentration in NYC and SF</p></li></ul><h3>Role Targeting Strategy</h3><ul><li><p>Primarily targeting mid to senior-level positions</p></li><li><p>Full-stack roles most commonly applied for</p></li><li><p>Increasing focus on AI/ML engineering roles</p></li><li><p>Platform and infrastructure roles as secondary focus</p></li></ul><h2>Recommendations for Follow-up</h2><h3>High-Priority Follow-ups</h3><ol><li><p><strong>Pending Interviews</strong>: Prepare for scheduled interviews</p></li><li><p><strong>Recent Applications</strong>: Monitor responses from August applications</p></li><li><p><strong>Recruiter Relationships</strong>: Maintain contact with active recruiters</p></li><li><p><strong>Company Research</strong>: Deep dive into companies showing interest</p></li></ol><h3>Application Strategy Optimization</h3><ul><li><p>Consider focusing on fewer, higher-quality applications</p></li><li><p>Tailor applications more specifically to company needs</p></li><li><p>Leverage recruiter relationships for warm introductions</p></li><li><p>Follow up on applications after 1-2 weeks</p></li></ul><hr><p><em>Report generated from "The Job Search Project.xlsx" data as of August 2025</em></p>
